From: Uke platform maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] regulator: admit exact Uke ADSP and GPU ARC resources

The live OEM Uke graph routes ADSP CX/MX to lcx.lvl/lmx.lvl and GPUCC
MXC to mxc.lvl. Admit these exact command-database resources through the
existing ARC implementation without substituting voltages or rail names.

diff --git a/drivers/regulator/qcom-rpmh-regulator-uke.c b/drivers/regulator/qcom-rpmh-regulator-uke.c
index d4a91c2..ec803ee 100644
--- a/drivers/regulator/qcom-rpmh-regulator-uke.c
+++ b/drivers/regulator/qcom-rpmh-regulator-uke.c
@@ -1991,9 +1991,12 @@ static int rpmh_regulator_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 		return rc;
 	}
 
-	/* OEM Uke supplies required by CPU, USB, UFS and WCN6750. */
+	/* OEM Uke supplies required by CPU, USB, UFS, WLAN, ADSP and GPU clocks. */
 	if (strcmp(aggr_vreg->resource_name, "cx.lvl") &&
 	    strcmp(aggr_vreg->resource_name, "mx.lvl") &&
+	    strcmp(aggr_vreg->resource_name, "lcx.lvl") &&
+	    strcmp(aggr_vreg->resource_name, "lmx.lvl") &&
+	    strcmp(aggr_vreg->resource_name, "mxc.lvl") &&
 	    strcmp(aggr_vreg->resource_name, "ldob2") &&
 	    strcmp(aggr_vreg->resource_name, "ldob4") &&
 	    strcmp(aggr_vreg->resource_name, "ldob7") &&
